{"name":"Blue Iguana","hex":"#539ccc","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"iguana","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A green iguana (Iguana iguana), a large tropical American lizard often kept as a pet.","Any member of the genus Iguana."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/iguana"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue iguana","blocks":[{"text":"The blue iguana, also known commonly as the Grand Cayman ground iguana, the Grand Cayman blue iguana, and the Cayman Island rock iguana, is an endangered species of lizard in the family Iguanidae. The species is endemic to the island of Grand Cayman. It was previously considered to be a subspecies of the Cuban iguana, Cyclura nubila, but in a 2004 article Frederic J. Burton reclassified it as a separate species because, according to him, the genetic differences discovered four years earlier between the different C. nubila populations warranted this interpretation. The blue iguana is one of the longest-living species of lizard."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Blue_iguana_%28Cyclura_lewisi%29_male.JPG/330px-Blue_iguana_%28Cyclura_lewisi%29_male.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_iguana"},{"title":"Blue Iguana (2018 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Iguana is a 2018 British romantic comedy thriller film written and directed by Hadi Hajaig. The film stars Sam Rockwell, Phoebe Fox, Danny Granger, Ben Schwartz, Peter Ferdinando, Simon Callow, Al Weaver, Robin Hellier, and Frances Barber."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/24/Blue_Iguana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Iguana_(2018_film)"},{"title":"Iguana","blocks":[{"text":"Iguana is a genus of herbivorous lizards that are native to tropical areas of Mexico, Central America, South America, and the Caribbean. The genus was first described by Austrian naturalist J.N. Laurenti in 1768. Two species are placed in the genus: The green iguana, which is widespread throughout its range and a popular pet; and the Lesser Antillean iguana, which is native to the Lesser Antilles. Genetic analysis indicates that the green iguana may comprise a complex of multiple species, some of which have been recently described, but the Reptile Database considers all of these as subspecies of the green iguana."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Green_Iguana_In_Florida.jpg/330px-Green_Iguana_In_Florida.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iguana"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Blue_Iguana_on_Wilderness_Trail_at_QEII_Botanic_Park.jpg/500px-Blue_Iguana_on_Wilderness_Trail_at_QEII_Botanic_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Blue_Iguana_on_Wilderness_Trail_at_QEII_Botanic_Park.jpg/1280px-Blue_Iguana_on_Wilderness_Trail_at_QEII_Botanic_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Blue_Iguana_on_Wilderness_Trail_at_QEII_Botanic_Park.jpg/500px-Blue_Iguana_on_Wilderness_Trail_at_QEII_Botanic_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blue iguana in forest off Wilderness Trail in Queen Elizabeth II Botanic Park, Grand Cayman","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_Iguana_on_Wilderness_Trail_at_QEII_Botanic_Park.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Grand_Cayman_blue_iguana.jpg/500px-Grand_Cayman_blue_iguana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Grand_Cayman_blue_iguana.jpg/1280px-Grand_Cayman_blue_iguana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Grand_Cayman_blue_iguana.jpg/500px-Grand_Cayman_blue_iguana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Grand Cayman blue iguana","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGrand_Cayman_blue_iguana.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/BlueIguanaFeb2010.jpg/500px-BlueIguanaFeb2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/